but now with our roles reversed.

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:01.630
Mr. President, we are ready
to launch our strike.

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:04.080
Please grant us the authorization to
undertake a full-scale attack.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:07.510
Mr. President, we don't
have any more time!

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:11.550
Might makes right, Mr. President!

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:13.820
We cannot hope to secure
international support

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.290
without a clear victory against
the Japanese!

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:18.450
The United States of America is a nation
that cannot tolerate defeat!

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:23.930
No, you are mistaken.

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:27.170
The United States of America owes
its responsibility to the world.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:29.440
It's over.

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:32.070
What we must do

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:35.880
is to lift the moratorium on grain
exports as of now.

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:38.740
I want this to be communicated
to all nations immediately.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.850
Mr. President!

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:46.040
Get me the CEO of Symbol right away.

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:49.150
I want to contact the leader of Japan.

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:51.630
Hirokawa here.

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:54.390
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs?

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:58.220
America is ending its moratorium
on grain exports immediately?

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:04.940
Right, give me more information
as it comes in.

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.840
To cast aside its hegemonic
power over the globe

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:11.470
and abandon its position as
leader of the world...

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:15.510
Alas, they chose the most arduous
path for themselves.

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:20.250
Hirokawa, call off all activities that
are part of our operation.

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:22.690
Deactivate the auto-start program.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:28.160
Why now? Even if America has
ended its moratorium...

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:31.130
But, Sir, this is a war we can win.

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:35.170
Yes!

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.530
The President of the United States?!

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:41.170
Master Nishida, it's the President
of the United States.

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:45.010
I am Nishida.

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:45.210
It seems that I will have to
be the first president
I am Nishida.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:47.150
It seems that I will have to
be the first president

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:51.480
in the history of the United States
to concede defeat.

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:56.110
No, that's not true. This was a war
where there could be no winner.

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:58.190
No winner?

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:02.360
It's true that now your nation has
abandoned hegemonism,

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:05.090
but that does not mean
your nation failed.

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:08.600
Has not failed? What do you mean?

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:12.300
We've called off all our plans for the
assault on the US economy.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.040
Nishida...

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:18.910
To set aside mistrust and deepen our
understanding of each other,

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:21.380
a simple act such as this is
rarely ever realized

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:24.940
in the field of politics and diplomacy,

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:28.360
but you were willing to do so.

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:33.860
I hope I might be able to
meet you one day.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:37.530
I too wish that I had had the
chance to meet you.

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:45.240
It is far harder to stop a war
than to start a war.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:49.530
I ask that all of you reflect
upon that fact in depth.

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:52.580
It seems that I've grown somewhat tired.

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:54.920
Please excuse me, as I must retire now.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.320
Yes, Sir. I will attend to any
outstanding issues.

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:45.090
Bring closure?

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:49.800
He wouldn't!

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:52.610
No, you don't mean to... Mr. Nishida!

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:09.680
Master Nishida!

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:14.220
Ideals are so very delicate.

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:19.400
Mr. Nishida, you've tried to bring
closure to this farce of a play

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:21.470
by taking your own life.

00:22:21.470 --> 00:22:27.270
But... Unfortunately, I'm not about to let
this farce end any time soon!

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:33.600
Hark

00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:40.150
It's time I journey

00:22:43.680 --> 00:22:50.820
Break apart my heart

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:57.350
For crimson sadness

00:22:57.680 --> 00:23:04.860
Pours out from it

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:08.780
I can only, oh

00:23:08.890 --> 00:23:11.970
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:12.060 --> 00:23:17.580
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:36.680
I can only, oh

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:39.830
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:39.900 --> 00:23:45.030
I pray, let this break apart

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:02.770
Thousands...

00:24:02.770 --> 00:24:06.670
No, returning after being adrift for
tens of thousands of years,

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:08.240
so that I might regain my time,

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:10.210
my life, to lead it to celebrate this life.

00:24:10.850 --> 00:24:12.650
Infinite power and immortality...

00:24:12.650 --> 00:24:15.620
They are nothing more than a mirage.

00:24:16.220 --> 00:24:19.740
Humans are born as humans, and
they shall die as humans.

00:24:20.550 --> 00:24:21.990
Letter from afar

00:24:21.990 --> 00:24:24.530
Known as Gasara, I cast
you aside in spite

00:24:24.530 --> 00:24:27.690
For thou art a cursed message,
circulated between us
